## 5. What to do when a release is bad

<!-- DECIDE: the actual mechanism per platform — staged rollout halt, phased
     release pause, expedited review. Note plainly what cannot be undone: a build
     already downloaded stays downloaded. -->

**Convention: cut forward, never move a tag, attach a release note.** The fix
is a new version, not a rewind or a retagged old one. See
`fragments/ROLLBACK-CONVENTION.md.template` for the fixed statement of this
convention plus the `<!-- DECIDE -->` markers this project fills in — who can
declare a release bad, who has authority to cut the rollback, and where the
incident gets recorded.

